 and his Helm leaving him  powerless on the floor and because of  his imprisonment the waking world starts  going through a terrifying situation A  disease known as the Sleepy sickness  breaks out the next morning we see that  over 1 million men women and children  never woke up from their dreams meaning  they died in their sleep that afternoon  the nightmare Corinthian tracks down  lord Mages and gives him advice on how  to keep Morpheus captive because if he  escapes he'll come for them both they'll  need to trap him inside a glass sphere  which itself is inside a binding Circle  to contain morpheus's physical  manifestation Corinthian also advises  Magis to make his guards take stimulants  to ensure they never fall asleep in  morpheus's presence because if they do  he will enter their dreams and control  them at last Corinthian tells Mages to  get rid of morpheus's Raven as she will  do whatever it takes to free him later  Mages heads to the basement where  Morpheus has been imprisoned and asks  him to return his son however the king  of Dreams remains silent and naked and  barely even moves his body to respond to  the questions the same routine continues  for for nearly a decade but Morpheus  still hasn't uttered a word during this  time Mages Second Son Alex Goes  increasingly curious about the prisoner  and even tries to help him get out  however Morpheus only remains silent  narrating to himself that he cannot give  what these humans want the wish will  only disrupt both the waking and the  dreaming worlds it is now 1926 and  morpheus's stole Investments have  created Youth and prosperity for Mages  and his followers one day Alex  approaches Morpheus and again explains  how his father would let him out if he  returned his dead son unfortunately  Mages catches his son talking to  Morpheus and punishes him for doing so  he then blackmails Alex into killing the  Raven and the boy reluctantly lures the  bird into morpheus's cage and shoots it  dead a devastated M