however she  shrugs him off and leaves saying that  she has an exorcism to deal with then  she goes into a church where she learns  that a rich princess is trying to marry  a footballer expectedly Johanna is  confused as to why the couple would  require an exorcism but just then she  hears the princess screaming it turns  out the football player has been  possessed and soon a demon climbs out of  his mouth it completely eviscerates the  football player and turns its attention  on Johanna Morpheus also arrives at the  same time and recognizes the demon the  two then begin conversing but  Constantine takes advantage of the  distraction and exercises the demon back  to Hell following the incident  Constantine and Morpheus finally have a  proper conversation outside where he  asks about his pouch of sand but to his  dismay Johanna reveals that she couldn't  open the drawstring so she sold it  Morpheus insists they must find the  pouch because his realm will cease to  exist otherwise if dreams disappear  destruction will follow however Johanna  does not pay heed to what he is saying  and walks away after the two-part waste  Morpheus notices a raven that has been  sent by Lucian to assist him the bird  introduces himself as Matthew and vows  to protect Morpheus at any cost next we  see Morpheus arriving in johanna's  dreams she appears to be having a  nightmare where a demon is trying to  drag her to hell just then she wakes up  and finds Morpheus in her room he  explains the detractor through a dream  and wants to help her since Constantine  experiences nightmares almost every  night Morpheus promises to get rid of  them this finally convinces her and she  begins looking for the sand pouch as she  looks in her office Morpheus finds  pictures of Johanna with her girlfriend  Rachel this triggers something in  Johanna and she realizes that the sand  pouch is actually at her girlfriend's  place in the next scene the two head to  Rachel's house to retrieve the pouch  Johanna explains that she used to live  there not long ago however when all the  people close to her started dying one  after another she decided to leave  Rachel to keep her safe soon the two  enter the house and are taken aback to  find Rachel under the spell of the sand  pouch her condition is so fragile that  she cannot even speak turns out she has  become addicted to the sand and the  dreams that come from it causing her  body to wither away as Morpheus  retrieves the sand patch from Rachel he  explains it wasn't meant for humans he  then prepares to leave but Constantine  demands he help her ex-girlfriend since  it was his sand that ruined her Morpheus  degrees and asks her to wait outside he  then pours sand over Rachel and puts her  out of her suffering it allows her to  have one last peaceful dream of Johanna  before she passes away back in Buffalo  Ethel reveals to her son that she only  stole the magical weapons because she  thought they'd help when Mages men came  after them she hid the Ruby and traded  the others for the mysterious amulet of  protection around her neck it has kept  her alive all these years but now she  doesn't want to continue any longer  hence she wants to return the Ruby to  Morpheus in hopes that he'll forgive  them however Jon wonders if they should  give it away when they could use it to  dream of a world without the king of  Dreams himself in reply Athol reveals  that many people have already died for  the Ruby and it's not worth keeping she  then takes off her Amulet of protection  and gives it to Jon as a peace offering  Ethel explains that it kept her alive  for 116 years so it should keep him  alive forever with the amulet now gone  her body begins to age rapidly and she  dies in John's arms leaving him  devastated hearing screams a guard  arrives and Witnesses the corpse he  quickly assumes that Jon has murdered  her and fires a bullet at him but  surprisingly because of the Amulet of  protection the bullet bounces back and  kills the guard instead after this Jon  walks out of the building which has been  keeping him captive for years as he  stands in the cold Buffalo streets the  Corinthian appears from behind and lends  him a coat Jon who thinks the man is  simply a stranger says that he doesn't  want it but Corinthian insists the final  scene shows Morpheus informing Johanna  of her ex-girlfriend's peaceful passing  in her sleep he also reassures her that  she won't be experiencing any Nightmares  From now on after she leaves Morpheus  and his new Raven friend Matthew discuss  their next move to go to hell this show  kicks ass be sure to catch the following  episodes on series Recaps
 

